package org.kruskopf.backend.section;

/**
 * One small, individually titled note — a "section" of a ship or a character.
 * <p>
 * A section is deliberately not a document: {@code body} is plain text, not
 * markdown, and there is no schema beyond the three fields. The list a section
 * belongs to is ordered as the user arranged it, and that order is the order the
 * JSON array is stored in — there is no ordering column.
 * <p>
 * {@code id} is generated by the client when the section is created and is
 * opaque here: it exists so the UI can address one section for an inline edit or
 * a delete without relying on its position. Nothing on the server reads it.
 * <p>
 * Shared by {@code Ship} and {@code GameCharacter} (see
 * {@link org.kruskopf.backend.json.SectionListConverter}), because a section
 * means the same thing in both places.
 */
public record ContentSection(
        String id,
        String title,
        String body
) {
}
